suggestion: `StatusCodeFromError` uses a direct type assertion (`err.(statusCoder)`) which won't extract the status code from wrapped errors. Since Go 1.20+ `errors.As` supports interface targets, consider:

```go
var sc statusCoder
if errors.As(err, &sc) {
    code := sc.StatusCode()
    if code >= 100 && code < 600 {
        return code, true
    }
}
```

This makes the instrumentation resilient to future linodego changes that might wrap errors (e.g. `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", linodegoErr)`) without breaking status code extraction.

